From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:32:11 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] wxGUI/nviz: the stereo separation is the person's depth
 limits

The two eyes are as far apart as the person's depth limits allow, and no
farther: the desktop gives the 3D view's window the limits set once for the
screen (Stereo KWin's 3D Depth settings, read through libstereo-declare in
the pixels of the view), a first pass from the camera between the eyes reads
how near and how far the pixels of the scene are, and the separation is the
largest under which every one of them stays inside the limits.  The limits
are read again four times a second while the view shows 3D.  Without limits
the eyes are the same picture and the console says why, once.

The eye separation setting is gone.  The 3D view's options are "Enable 3D",
on unless the person turns it off, and a button to the display settings,
where each screen's 3D mode, output and eye order are chosen.  On a screen
with no stereo visual the view stays one picture without a word; it is said
only when the person ticks Enable 3D there.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
